// @run
// @log 255
// Regression (silent-class-inventory D1008), graduated from
// `error-u8-field-through-generic-alias.vl`.
//
// THE GENERIC-ALIAS SPELLING of `arrays/u8-struct-field.vl`. The two files pinned the SAME
// sentence on purpose — one field, two spellings, and the only thing that may distinguish
// them is which one a reader typed — so they close together too. `type Box<T> = { v: T }` at
// `Box<u8[]>` reaches a DIFFERENT interner (`gaeEnsure`, not `collectS`), and before #1829
// that one read the same -1 and returned quietly: check-clean invalid wasm on the program
// the direct spelling refused in one line.
//
// This one WRITES the field and reads it back (`b.v = [255]`), so the log is the value and
// not merely a compile — a field code that interned the wrong backing would not survive a
// 255 through a one-byte store.
type Box<T> = { v: T }

const b: Box<u8[]> = { v: [7] }
b.v = [255]
print(b.v[0])
